---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Agent Skills | Wyatt Entrekin">
  <section class="project-shell">
    <a class="back-link reveal" href="/projects"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Projects</a>

    <section class="project-hero reveal glass-card">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="hero-kicker">Active Project</p>
        <h1>Agent Skills</h1>
        <p class="hero-text">
          My custom AI coding framework that integrates an agentic /work command natively into Claude Code, OpenAI
          Codex, and Google Antigravity
        </p>
        <div class="hero-tags">
          <span>Agentic Workflows</span>
          <span>Developer Tooling</span>
          <span>Claude Code</span>
          <span>OpenAI Codex</span>
          <span>Google Antigravity</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <span class="status-pill">Active</span>
        <a
          class="icon-link"
          href="https://github.com/wmentrekin/agent-skills"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
          aria-label="GitHub Repository"
          title="GitHub Repository"
        >
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path
              d="M12 2C6.48 2 2 6.58 2 12.24c0 4.53 2.87 8.37 6.84 9.73.5.09.68-.22.68-.49 0-.24-.01-1.05-.01-1.9-2.78.62-3.37-1.21-3.37-1.21-.45-1.18-1.11-1.49-1.11-1.49-.91-.64.07-.63.07-.63 1 .07 1.53 1.05 1.53 1.05.9 1.57 2.36 1.12 2.94.86.09-.67.35-1.12.63-1.38-2.22-.26-4.55-1.14-4.55-5.06 0-1.12.39-2.03 1.03-2.75-.1-.26-.45-1.31.1-2.73 0 0 .84-.28 2.75 1.05A9.3 9.3 0 0 1 12 6.86c.85 0 1.71.12 2.51.35 1.91-1.33 2.75-1.05 2.75-1.05.55 1.42.2 2.47.1 2.73.64.72 1.03 1.63 1.03 2.75 0 3.93-2.33 4.8-4.56 5.05.36.32.68.95.68 1.92 0 1.39-.01 2.5-.01 2.84 0 .27.18.59.69.49A10.13 10.13 0 0 0 22 12.24C22 6.58 17.52 2 12 2Z"
              fill="currentColor"
            ></path>
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="info-card reveal glass-card">
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Agent Skills is a shared workflow framework for AI coding agents, distributed as a single directory (
        <code>.agents/</code>) that gets imported into any project repo via <code>git subtree</code>. Instead of
        re-explaining how I want an agent to work every time I start a new project, or maintaining separate,
        drifting conventions per repo, I built this once as its own canonical repository and pull it into each
        project I work on, this site included. Every repo that imports it gets the same single entry point,
        <code>/work</code>, and that command behaves identically whether I'm driving it from Claude Code, OpenAI
        Codex, or Google Antigravity. Each of those tools discovers the workflow through its own native mechanism
        (a symlinked skill for Claude Code and Codex, direct file reads for Antigravity), but they're all reading
        the exact same source of truth, so the underlying behavior never forks across tools.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        The core idea is an orchestrator model. A single outward-facing agent owns the conversation with me end to
        end, but it isn't the one doing most of the actual work. It classifies the request, decides which of
        four internal stages it's in (discovery, planning, execution, verification), and spawns narrowly-scoped
        subagents to do the real digging and building. Discovery is handled by research agents that ground
        everything in actual repo state or current external facts rather than assumption. Execution is routed by
        domain so there's no single generic "developer" persona; a task gets handed to whichever specialist
        actually fits it (data engineering, frontend, platform, ML operations, and so on), with an explicit
        fallback role for anything that doesn't cleanly match. The size of the request matters too: a one-line fix
        gets handled directly, while anything with real ambiguity or a large surface area gets a durable
        requirements document, a written plan, and an execution log, all stored as YAML files under
        <code>docs/&lt;feature&gt;/</code> in the project repo itself, so the state of the work survives context
        resets and a fresh agent (or a human) can pick up exactly where things left off.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        Verification isn't optional or self-reported. Once execution opens a pull request, dedicated reviewer and
        tester agents run against the real diff and post actual findings as PR review comments, not just a summary
        in chat. Anywhere the workflow needs to loop back and correct itself, a failed review, a failed
        test, etc., it's capped at two cycles before it has to stop and hand the decision back to me instead of
        spinning indefinitely. And before any code changes are ever made, there's a mandatory checkpoint: the
        agent has to explicitly ask whether to proceed, revise the plan, narrow the scope, or stop. That checkpoint
        is deliberately placed at the one moment that matters most, before anything is actually built,
        rather than asking for approval after the fact.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        The theme underneath all of this is that I wanted an agent to behave less like a single freeform chat
        session and more like a small, disciplined engineering team: defined roles, a real paper trail, explicit
        handoffs between stages, and built-in limits against runaway or unsupervised behavior. Centralizing it as
        one importable repo also means it actually improves over time, when I refine a convention or fix a
        gap in the workflow, I update it once and pull the change into every project that uses it, instead of
        patching the same idea slightly differently across a dozen repos.
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>

  <style>
    .project-shell {
      display: grid;
      gap: 1rem;
      padding-top: 0.8rem;
    }

    .project-hero {
      display: flex;
      align-items: flex-start;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 1rem;
      padding: 1.05rem 1.15rem;
    }

    .hero-kicker {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--text-soft);
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.74rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .hero-copy h1 {
      margin: 0.35rem 0 0.45rem;
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.2rem);
      line-height: 0.96;
      letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    }

    .hero-text {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.98rem;
      line-height: 1.65;
      max-width: 34rem;
      text-wrap: pretty;
    }

    .hero-tags {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.45rem;
      margin-top: 0.8rem;
    }

    .hero-tags span {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 1.75rem;
      padding: 0.1rem 0.58rem;
      border-radius: 999px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
      color: var(--text-soft);
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .hero-actions {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.55rem;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }

    .status-pill {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 1.85rem;
      padding: 0.14rem 0.68rem;
      border-radius: 999px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.09);
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
      color: var(--text-soft);
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .icon-link {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      width: 1.85rem;
      height: 1.85rem;
      padding: 0;
      border-radius: 999px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
      color: var(--text);
      text-decoration: none;
      flex-shrink: 0;
      transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease, border-color 180ms ease;
    }

    .icon-link:hover {
      color: var(--text);
      border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
      transform: translateY(-3px);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-hover);
    }

    .icon-link svg {
      width: 0.95rem;
      height: 0.95rem;
      flex: 0 0 auto;
    }

    .construction-note {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      line-height: 1.55;
    }

    .construction-note strong {
      display: inline-block;
      color: var(--text-soft);
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-right: 0.5rem;
    }

    .info-card {
      padding: 1.3rem;
    }

    .info-card h2 {
      margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 1.55rem;
      line-height: 1;
      letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    }

    .info-card p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .info-card p + p {
      margin-top: 0.85rem;
    }

    .info-card code {
      padding: 0.08rem 0.32rem;
      border-radius: 0.35rem;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
      color: var(--text-soft);
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.85em;
    }

    @media (max-width: 920px) {
      .project-hero {
        flex-direction: column;
      }
    }

    @media (max-width: 480px) {
      .info-card {
        padding: 1rem;
      }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
